<title>UK: GEC sells Satchwell to Siebe.</title>
<headline>GEC sells Satchwell to Siebe.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering and defence group General Electric Co Plc said on Thursday that it had sold Satchwell Controls to Siebe Plc for 80 million stg.  </p>
<p>GEC said that Satchwell Controls is the UK's largest manufacturer and installer of building automation systems for industrial and commercial facilities.</p>
<p>The company said the sale was part of a disposal programme announced in December 1996.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
